WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
At the end of the Passover
meal, Jewish families say:

2
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.790
next year in Jerusalem.

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.860
Three times a day, the Amidah prayer
asks God to gather the exiles and rebuild

4
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.120
Jerusalem.

5
00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:16.590
For centuries, the return was left
to God and the days of the Messiah.

6
00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.970
Then, in 1897, about 200 delegates
met in a hall in Basel, Switzerland.

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:29.550
After 1,800 years of prayer, why did
a modern movement decide not to wait?

8
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.970
In this mission, you'll read
a prophet's promise of return,

9
00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.690
and follow a famous trial in Paris.

10
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:40.260
Then you'll go back to Basel, and see
what the delegates set out to build.

11
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:45.250
Your mission: find out why a modern
movement decided not to wait for the return

12
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.030
to Zion.
